<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-18401] Sql. Different behavior of float cost approach leads to failed test. </title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-18401</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Test like:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
query IIIII
SELECT 127::DECIMAL(3,0)::FLOAT, -17014118346046923173168730371588410572::DECIMAL(38,0)::FLOAT, -7::DECIMAL(9,1)::FLOAT, 27::DECIMAL(18,1)::FLOAT, 33::DECIMAL(38,1)::FLOAT
----
127  -1.7014119E37  -7 27 33 

[row=0, col=1, expected=-1.7014119E37, actual=-1.701412E37]&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;failed in ai-3 and passed in ai-2 cause in ai-2 in case of one fragment it always plans into local node &lt;em&gt;without&lt;/em&gt; any serialization\deserialization usage against ai-3 approach: through serialization, thus we obtain in ai-2 approach only&#160;&lt;br/&gt;
ExpressionFactoryImpl#compile &lt;del&gt;{&lt;/del&gt;}&amp;gt; ConstantExpression#write (case FLOAT) branch, while&#160; in ai{-}3: float was trimmed a bit in org.apache.calcite.rex.RexBuilder#clean and after goes into ExpressionFactoryImpl and so on ..&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Need further investigation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
